WEBVTT

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.490
<i>Illya-chan...</i>

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:14.910
W-Wait... Time out...

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.490
Give me more of your saliva...

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.910
It's not my place to say anything.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.630
That dream again?

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.640
Why do I keep having that same dream?

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.730
That one...

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:41.640
Where Illya-chan, Miyu-chan, 
and Kuro-chan all...

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.650
They're lewd! They're all too lewd!

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.410
I can't sleep...

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:55.150
If this keeps up, I'm gonna lose it.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:00.850
I need to expel these dirty feelings somehow!

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.680
Looks like my only choice is to write it out.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:41.990
<b>Episode 3
Girls, Life Is Short, so Rot Away</b>

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.960
I feel like we're not getting very far.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.730
What? You're the one who said we should 
all get together to do our homework.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.740
I know, but...

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.680
Illya, hang in there.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.800
If you systematically start taking care of it now,

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.070
you won't have it so hard on the last day of break.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.700
But I kind of get it, though.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.810
You just can't get into the mood 
for homework this early in the break.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.130
Right?

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.040
That's how failures think of it.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.210
Illya, Miyu's right.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.030
Huh?

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.710
If you start systematically working on it early,

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:22.840
you won't have it so hard at the last minute.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.430
It's important to get things done early.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:28.160
Wh-What's gotten into you, Suzuka?

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.100
That's unlike you to say.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.820
If only I'd started earlier, 
I wouldn't be down to the wire...

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.520
A deadline that's not tight isn't a deadline!

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.700
I've learned many things...

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.250
Wh-What happened to you?

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.290
Did the heat drive you crazy?

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:56.530
You can say that, but it still 
doesn't help motivate us.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:59.300
Besides, Tattsun isn't even here.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:02.820
Tatsuko said she had to prepare for the festival.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.330
Festival?

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:07.590
You know, the summer festival next weekend.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.780
When I get home,

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:14.560
I need to help my sister get ready 
for the summer festival again...

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.770
I get the feeling you're talking about 
a different summer festival.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:21.560
Oh, that's right.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:24.150
Why don't we all go to the festival together?

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:25.970
Oh, sounds good!

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.100
I agree!

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.930
Not a bad idea.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:32.540
Yes, I'd like to go with you, Illya.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:35.140
If we do that, I want to wear a yukata.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.940
Yukata? You mean like you wear at hot springs?

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:40.380
No, those are also called "yukata," but...

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.420
<b>Main Characters: Normal girls           Cute Type 

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:43.420
The yukata worn for festivals are different.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.850
How about you, Mimi?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.400
Want to go to the festival with...

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:52.400
M-Mimi, what's wrong? 
You seem a bit down...

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.940
N-No, I'm fine! I just haven't slept very well...

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.690
Haven't slept?

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.320
Are you worried about something?

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.490
It's not a big deal. It's just...

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:04.530
It's just?

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.650
The characters won't behave the way I want,

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.800
and I can't make their actions convincing...

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.160
And their motives are unclear to start with...

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.930
Huh? Wh-What are you talking about?

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:17.290
A Japanese assignment?

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.190
Free research?

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:24.350
If it's something that difficult, 
let's think about it together!

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:25.480
What's it about?

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:27.150
I-It's fine!

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.170
I'll do something about it on my own!

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:32.320
But as long as we're all here...

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:34.310
I-It's really all right!

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:36.960
Don't say that...

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:36.960
Illya,

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:41.160
she said she'd handle it herself, 
so I don't think we should force her...

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:45.900
Huh? But if a friend's in trouble, 
shouldn't we help?

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:49.100
I think it depends on the situation.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.290
Sometimes you don't want to trouble them,
because they're your friends.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.750
I wonder about that.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.060
Kuro?

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:03.220
It's up to them to decide if 
it's a bother or not, right?

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:07.120
I don't think it's right to decide that it's 
a bother before you even talk about it.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:08.940
But in some cases,

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:11.320
the moment you bring it up, 
it's a bother to them.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:15.180
I'm saying, you don't know that
until you talk about it, right?

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:17.890
But that would be retroactive approval.

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:19.730
I couldn't do that to a friend.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.290
You're wrong. It's because they're a friend—

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:25.440
H-Hold on, calm down, you two!

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:29.730
What? Do you share Miyu's opinion?

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:30.450
Huh?

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:32.370
Which is it?

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:36.300
If they want to hide something,

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:39.240
I don't think it's right to force them to share it...

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:43.460
But if they're a friend, I'd want them 
to talk to me about it, I guess...

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:47.440
What kind of vague answer is that? 
That's the problem with you!

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.450
They're getting awfully heated up.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:49.870
Kuro, you shouldn't blame Illya.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:51.500
I've thought this for a while,

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:52.640
You and I were the ones talking.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.220
but there's something strange 
about those three, isn't there?

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:56.730
Hmph... You're always quick to cover for Illya.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.730
It's like there's something we don't know.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.650
Oh, maybe it's you-know-what?

00:06:56.730 --> 00:07:00.280
Is that how you define your friendship?

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:01.850
Like, they're arguing over Illya's brother?

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:04.650
Ah... The pain of being a woman.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:08.110
This wouldn't happen if they were all guys.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.360
<i>That's it.</i>

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:16.570
<i>If I can't write them well as girls, then...</i>

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:16.200
Cut it out, you two!

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.420
<i>If they were boys...</i>

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.190
<i>Be mine, Mimi.</i>

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:27.270
<i>Kuro! How could you, 
when you already have me?</i>

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:32.330
<i>Illyas... Even if my feelings never 
reach you, I'll stay beside you.</i>

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:36.100
Th-This should work!

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:43.370
I don't quite get it, but it 
seems like things are resolved.

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:46.720
Hey, Mimi's going to be okay!

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:49.690
Let's get this done so we can play!

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:54.940
Huh? Mimi, what happened 
to you all of a sudden?

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:57.680
She seems kind of unapproachable.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.620
Did something happen?

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.960
We don't know, either.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:07.920
I'm home.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:10.880
Welcome back.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.460
O-Onee... Did something happen?

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:17.890
Suzuka, draw twelve pages of manga right now.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.350
Huh? That's impossible, and you know it!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:23.180
You said this morning that 
you only had touch-ups left!

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:24.180
She dropped it.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:24.900
Huh?

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.230
That damn Akira dropped it!

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:29.720
We were going to do a twelve-page 
manuscript together, and she dropped it!

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:31.190
So you draw it!

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:32.840
I can't do that!

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:34.410
Use some common sense, you idiot!

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:39.040
I don't live within the 
boundaries of common sense!

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.760
Anyway, just prepare the manuscript!

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:43.250
I don't care if it's a manga or a short story!

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:46.360
You think I just happen to have 
a manga or story lying around—

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:49.070
Wait, I might.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:52.600
You want to continue our study group now?

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:55.840
Huh? I should bring all my notebooks?

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.930
Sure, that's fine...

00:08:58.130 --> 00:08:59.450
Let me see...

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:01.270
"Forbidden Quartet."

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:04.810
A reverse harem story, with three 
bisexual men in a relationship!

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:05.910
This is nice.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:10.570
I can feel the imagination 
boiling up from the pages!

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:12.940
I see, I see...

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:17.320
Please, Mimi! Let us publish this short story!

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.540
It must have been tough,

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:27.170
holding so much imagination inside.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:29.730
We know.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:32.920
We know how hard it can be to keep 
your overflowing thoughts hidden.

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:36.730
But we also understand your feelings.

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:39.650
That's right. We're comrades.

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:45.160
Mimi, we wouldn't do anything bad with it.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:50.480
Will you entrust us with those feelings 
and the story you wrote?

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:06.910
W-W-Welcome!

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:11.330
Yes, yes, that's it. It's only embarrassing at first.

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:14.930
Everyone around you is a fellow comrade, 
so there's no need to be embarrassed.

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:17.340
W-Welcome!

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:18.970
Welcome!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:20.970
Welcome!

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:22.910
Nice, nice!

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:24.760
You have talent, Mimi!

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.520
It started out as yuri.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:34.980
What are you talking about?

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:39.660
In her notebook, she'd 
written a lovely lesbian story

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:41.520
about characters based on all of you.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:42.450
Huh?

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:48.060
But it probably didn't feel intimate— 
I mean, fitting enough to her.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.210
So she changed the characters' sexes,

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:53.130
and her soul rotted at light speed, and she fell.

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:53.530
Huh?

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:56.450
Ever since, she's been rolling downhill, 
getting more hooked on our rotten world.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:55.660
Her soul rotted?

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:58.440
It's like she's stuck in muck up to her neck.

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:00.280
Ah, but it's for a general audience right now.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:02.870
For now, she's doing relatively 
soft stuff for a general audience,

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.720
so you don't have to worry.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:08.740
Wait, how is BL fit for a general audience? 
I can't believe I said that myself!

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:13.460
Please, let up on the gas a little!

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:17.280
You're using nothing but suspicious vocabulary, 
and I can't understand you!

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:20.530
Seriously, what are you talking 
about? What is all this?

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.210
It's about Mimi.

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:26.290
Mimi?

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:27.660
What happened to Mimi?

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:29.410
She's become a fujoshi.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.620
A fujoshi?

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:33.130
Yes, a fujoshi. A rotten woman.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:34.790
A rotten woman?

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.300
Well, I'm pretty rotten, too.

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:42.380
Argh, jeez! Explaining it is getting us nowhere!

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:45.310
Come to my place and I'll show 
you what I'm talking about!

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:53.870
Wow.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:55.540
There are so many books.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:57.070
Impressive.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:59.100
Are all these yours, Suzuka?

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.630
No, about 80% are Onee's.

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:04.560
She uses my room as her library.

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:06.950
Anyway, sit wherever you like.

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:11.760
So, to be frank, I'm what they call a "fujoshi."

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:14.330
It means I'm someone who 
likes what's known as "BL."

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:15.220
B?

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:15.960
L?

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:19.710
I guess I have to start there, huh?

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.500
Uh...

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:27.340
Crap! Mimi's already here!

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:28.760
You called Mimi over, too?

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:31.020
For now, just hide in the closet!

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:33.560
Why?

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.150
Just see how Mimi acts for yourselves.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:40.280
And as for what BL is, you'll figure
it out when you read this.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:41.400
Huh?

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:46.110
I'm going to bring Mimi in. Just keep quiet!

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:50.450
What the heck is this about?

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:51.940
Pardon me.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.200
Have a seat anywhere.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:55.940
Okay.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:58.790
Mimi...

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.530
She doesn't seem any different than usual.

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:04.700
Does that mean it isn't her 
appearance that changed?

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:09.810
So, hey! That book you lent me was really good!

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:11.370
Y-Yeah?

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:15.220
At first, Scarecrow-sama was being timid, 
so I thought it might be a riba.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:19.860
But later, when Dolphin's sasoi-uke lit 
the flames between them, I just...

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:22.860
Y-Yeah, I know!

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:24.560
What are they saying?

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:26.740
I think they're talking about BL.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.260
Hmm...

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:30.450
If we try reading that, we might understand.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:31.950
Oh, right.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:34.660
It's pretty thin for a book, though...

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:34.660
<b>Just Friends</b>

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:36.340
Let's see...

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.170
Wait...

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:56.440
Isn't this what standard Japanese would call...

00:13:56.790 --> 00:13:58.470
A homo manga?!

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:01.440
Wh-Wh-Wha—

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:05.770
I see... BL... I've heard of this.

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:07.200
K-Kuro?

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:08.910
Boy's Love.

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:14.070
A beautiful, fleeting world that 
depicts love between men.

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:19.520
Because their relationship is forbidden, 
their love burns ever pure.

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:24.830
Further, most people refer to 
derivative works as "Yaoi,"

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:29.270
which is slightly different from commercial BL, 
but not really different for our purposes.

00:14:29.270 --> 00:14:31.300
Why do you know so much about it, Kuro?

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:35.260
So, then! Scarecrow-sama's Exc***bur 
grew e**** as his s***** urges

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:40.380
****ed, and when they finally b***ed 
each other, it was c*********!

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:44.150
Right? You think so too, right? 
It has to be that way, right?

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:44.150
Hey, calm down, Mimi, okay?

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:49.100
When th*** b****s e*****ed, to e***** 
t**** l***, it was ***, a **** ***!

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:51.870
Y-Yeah, I know.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:55.680
N-No way... Mimi, our honor student,

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:58.910
is using so many terms that require 
educational discretion!

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:06.000
She sounds like Berserker now.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:10.180
I can't watch anymore! I have to stop Mimi!

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:10.180
Wait!

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:12.640
This is interesting, so let's watch a little more!

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:16.160
Uh-huh! And then! Scarecrow-sama—

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:14.640
Don't stop me!

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.600
Hey! If you move, the door will come off!

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:17.600
Huh? Wh-What?

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.530
Look, Mimi...

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:25.860
This isn't...

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:31.490
Wh-What were you doing inside 
the closet to get so sweaty?

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:34.660
Her thoughts are completely pink!

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:38.430
So, as you can see, it's already out of control,

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:40.950
so I wanted to ask for your help.

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:42.600
That's cruel, Suzuka-chan.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.670
You outed me to them...

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.350
But why did you suddenly...

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:49.140
Were you always like this?

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:50.550
N-No!

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:57.600
Um... I only recently started writing BL stories...

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:01.520
And I hadn't even shown them to 
anyone, but then Suzuka-chan...

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:04.370
I ran her BL story in our book at ComiMa!

00:16:04.370 --> 00:16:08.280
Then it was clearly you who 
dragged Mimi down this path!

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.210
I couldn't help it!

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:14.550
The panic of the battlefield and the 
thrill of the event drove us to madness!

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.910
It's Mimi's tastes that have gone mad!

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:19.700
Stop it! Don't blame Suzuka-chan!

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:21.960
M-Mimi?

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.010
It's not anyone's fault.

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:26.960
I wrote those stories according to my own tastes.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:29.300
Suzuka-chan just gave me an opportunity.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:30.540
Mimi...

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:34.760
It just means I... My...

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:39.730
My soul was already shaped by BL...

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:41.870
Come back, Mimi!

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:48.000
Just seeing two men walking together on 
the street makes my heart start racing.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.090
She's terminal.

00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:51.280
No, for fujoshi, that's a basic skill.

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:56.740
Lately, I can't stop having lewd thoughts 
about Shirou-san and Issei-san!

00:16:56.970 --> 00:17:00.110
I've filled twelve notebooks 
with short stories about them!

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:00.950
No!

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:03.230
Even Onii-chan's fallen victim?!

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:04.110
You're telling me to fight with this worn-out bat?

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:04.620
You've really done it now.

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:07.830
Hmph. What's wrong with a well-used bat?

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.510
So which is the seme?

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:07.880
What are you saying, Kuro?

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:12.320
If the tool changes how well you perform, 
that shows how limited your skill is.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:12.320
I can only see Shirou-san as a hetare-seme 
and Issei-sama as an oshikake-uke.

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:14.750
Seriously, what are you saying, Mimi?

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:17.870
Why? Why do you always get in my way?

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:16.880
Please, wake up already!

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:20.630
Two men doing that is just not right!

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:21.470
Do you hate me that much?

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:23.810
It's because it isn't right that it's pure love! 
Why can't you understand?

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.810
If only it were hate...

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:25.940
How could I understand that?!

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:28.830
Shut up, you rugrats!

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:31.920
Onee!

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:34.320
Enough with the squeaking and squawking!

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:36.240
S-Suzuka's older sister?

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:37.380
Onee-sama?

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:38.280
Onee-sama?!

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:41.060
Huh? What's this sensation?

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:42.700
This feeling of bottomless emptiness?

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:46.830
Wow, you can sense Onee's rotten aura, too?

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.300
Onee is on a completely different level from us.

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:51.190
She's a higher breed known as "kifujin"!

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:53.840
Now it's just one strange term after another!

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:55.370
For crying out loud...

00:17:56.260 --> 00:18:01.170
You interrupted me when I was in the closet playing 
a BL drama CD for some simulated voyeurism!

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:03.220
You're right! She's on a completely different level!

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.230
Hey, Mimi...

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:05.350
Y-Yes?

00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:07.630
How does it feel, being outed to your friends?

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:09.150
Huh? Uh...

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:10.780
Well...

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:16.820
I-It's really embarrassing.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:18.780
But...

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:22.990
I can't help but like BL!

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:24.270
Mimi...

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:25.330
And?

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:27.790
What do you young ladies want to do?

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:34.020
I don't really think it's normal 
for guys to be together...

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:37.250
So I'd like her to stop with the BL.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:39.370
Hmm, I see.

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:41.890
I don't really care.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:45.310
Well, then, it's simple. You two...

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:46.600
stop being friends.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:47.600
Huh?

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:49.990
Hey... Onee, that's...

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:51.930
Well, that's how it is, right?

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:54.940
Telling someone to stop something 
because you don't understand...

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:58.070
Who wants a friend like that, right?

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:00.780
But... But...

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.250
It's weird, no matter how you look at it.

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:04.360
We know.

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:08.710
Mimi and I both know that 
without you telling us.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:09.790
Then...

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:13.620
It's true that BL is a strange 
and embarrassing hobby.

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:16.130
That's why we keep quiet about it.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:17.900
Suzuka?

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:20.130
Yes, I outed her.

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:22.850
It's a hobby we can't tell our 
parents and friends about.

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:27.060
But still, we can't just stop liking it.

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:31.270
Besides, is a friend someone who 
interferes just because it's weird?

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.980
Does friendship mean you reject 
things you don't understand?

00:19:35.930 --> 00:19:36.990
Screw that.

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:40.530
If you're a real friend, laugh away their shame!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:44.380
If you can't do that, 
at least pretend not to notice.

00:19:57.740 --> 00:20:00.170
What? Is that something to laugh about?

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:03.890
Well, what you're saying is crazy!

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:07.670
What you're saying is, "Stay out of it," right?

00:20:07.670 --> 00:20:10.350
Th-That's right! What's wrong with that?

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:12.580
Mimi...

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.770
I'm sorry for saying those things.

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:18.530
I was ignoring your feelings.

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:22.110
Illya-chan... You...

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:24.930
What's this? A "they made up" ending?

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:27.830
Onee, you stole the good parts.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:31.410
Well, that said, it's a hobby you 
want to keep hidden, right?

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:34.920
So you should probably tone it down a bit, Mimi.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:38.710
She's right. We're still kids, after all.

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:42.690
I'd rather you take your time 
getting to know BL, Mimi.

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:44.160
Suzuka-chan...

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:47.580
Because we've only just begun our descent

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:50.570
down the endless slippery slope that is BL.

00:20:50.570 --> 00:20:52.390
That road only goes down?

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:57.120
Wait, come to think of it, if you like 
seeing romance between men,

00:20:57.120 --> 00:21:01.400
does that mean girls who like BL 
have no interest in getting boyfriends?

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:05.070
No, no... BL is just a fantasy.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:08.370
It's completely separate from 
real love and marriage.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:11.410
Thank goodness! So in 
the future, even Mimi can...

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:14.790
What? I don't want a boyfriend!

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:18.480
Declaring you'll be alone forever 
at your age is way too sad.

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:22.380
Huh? No, I didn't mean it like that. I...

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:31.220
I think boys should date boys, 
and girls should date girls.

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:36.690
Huh?

00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:42.050
Well, we should be going.

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:43.560
We need to get home.

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:45.070
I have things to do, too.

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:46.810
Why are you all running away? Wait!

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:49.730
I kind of understand that.

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:35.960
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:21.400 --> 00:23:23.060
Let's play until it closes!

00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:24.460
Yeah!

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:28.420
Pictures in a wedding dress?

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:30.010
But be careful,

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:33.100
or you'll get lost in the parade 
and we'll never find you again.

00:23:33.100 --> 00:23:35.010
Initially climbing like this is—

00:23:33.280 --> 00:25:35.010
<b>Theme Park Panic!</b>
